{"id":"chatcmpl-614c2f3a-16b1-4ab6-9895-63add9271c2b","object":"chat.completion","created":1795229197,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates how to handle medical image interpretation when the image projection (lateral view) is inherently limited for determining laterality. The successful strategy involved consulting a domain expert tool with a targeted question that acknowledged the limitation, then combining the expert's answer with prior case memory to reach a confident conclusion. The key insight is that when direct visual evidence is ambiguous, leveraging specialized tools and contextual memory can resolve the uncertainty.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When image projection limits direct assessment of a property (e.g., laterality on a lateral view), query a domain-specific expert tool with a question that explicitly states the limitation to get a calibrated answer.\",\n    \"Combine expert tool outputs with prior case memory or contextual metadata to resolve ambiguities that the image alone cannot settle.\",\n    \"Before committing to an answer, identify whether the imaging modality/projection provides sufficient information for the specific finding; if not, seek alternate evidence sources rather than guessing from the image.\",\n    \"Frame expert queries to ask both about presence and about whether the property in question can be determined from the given view, enabling the expert to signal uncertainty.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Recognize projection limitations (lateral vs. AP/PA) and use expert consultation plus case context to determine laterality or hidden findings.\",\n    \"Ambiguous evidence resolution\": \"When primary evidence is insufficient, explicitly acknowledge the gap, query specialized tools with limitation-aware questions, and cross-reference with memory/context.\",\n    \"Tool-assisted decision making\": \"Design tool queries that ask about both the finding and the assessability of the finding, so the tool can express uncertainty rather than forcing a binary answer.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm whether the image projection/modality can actually support the required determination (e.g., laterality on a lateral view) before answering.\",\n    \"Cross-check expert tool output against prior case memory or contextual metadata before finalizing the answer.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":504,"total_tokens":915,"completion_tokens":411,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":504},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":411}}}